The boot layer's U-Boot code (abboot/), the board code (boards/) and the patches (uboot/patches/)
are built into U-Boot, which is GPL-2.0-or-later, and are under that license.

The tools meant to be copied into an operating system or run on a computer, tools/bootctl,
tools/abctl.py and examples/update-slot.sh, are under the MIT license (LICENSES/MIT.txt), so an
OS image can ship them whatever its own license. MIT is compatible with the GPL.

